  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nThe upper ridge starts to move eastward on Friday as the eastern \ntrough deamplifies flattening out the flow a bit into the weekend. \nThe surface high pressure also moves off to the east during the \ndaytime Friday. Several rounds of shortwave energy pass through the \nflow with moisture returning late Friday night into Saturday morning \non the nose of the low level jet (overnight Friday night). This will \nbring the return of shower and storm chances (20-40%) especially \nwest/north. Although there will be dry periods, active weather \ncontinues the later part of the weekend into early next week as well \nwith several additional chances for showers/storms. Temperatures \nbegin an upward climb again Saturday into Sunday with heat indices \nin the 90s on Sunday at this time range.",
